<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Churchill is a 78-year-old man five weeks after a minor right-hemisphere lacunar stroke, on clopidogrel, atorvastatin, amlodipine 10 mg, and lisinopril 5 mg, which was added two weeks ago. For three days, during the current heat wave, he has felt lightheaded and dim-sighted for a minute or so when he stands up, worst on rising from his afternoon nap and after dinner. Yesterday he had to sit back down on the edge of the bed to avoid falling; he did not fall or lose consciousness. The symptoms go away when he sits or lies down. He has had no new weakness, numbness, change in speech, facial droop, double vision, or vertigo, and his left arm and leg are no weaker than last week. He has had no chest pain or palpitations. He admits drinking less water than advised and still has whisky and soda through the afternoon and wine at dinner. His 30-day heart monitor is still in place. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Three days ago, two weeks after lisinopril was added, during hot weather</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>Lightheadedness and dimming of vision on standing; no spinning</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>About a minute each time</td></tr><tr><td>Timing</td><td>On rising, worst after his afternoon nap and after dinner</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>One near-fall without injury; no loss of consciousness</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Relieved by sitting or lying down; worse with heat, low fluid intake, and alcohol</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>Denies new focal weakness, numbness, speech change, facial droop, diplopia, vertigo, chest pain, and palpitations</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

