  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Orthostatic hypotension (I95.1)</content>. A fall of 22 mmHg systolic on standing, with symptoms, after adding lisinopril to amlodipine 10 mg, made worse by heat, low fluid intake, and alcohol. The symptoms are positional and the neurological examination is unchanged, so a transient ischemic attack is unlikely. Creatinine has risen from 0.98 to 1.12 mg/dL (eGFR 67) with potassium 4.6, consistent with low volume and the new ACE inhibitor. [S]<list><item>Reduce amlodipine from 10 mg to 5 mg daily; continue lisinopril 5 mg.</item><item>Drink about 2 liters of fluid a day during the hot weather, and keep alcohol out of the afternoon.</item><item>Sit on the edge of the bed for a minute before standing, especially after his nap and at night.</item><item>Home blood pressure seated and standing each morning; bring the readings to the next visit.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Essential hypertension (I10)</content>. Seated blood pressure 118/68 mmHg today is below target at the cost of orthostatic symptoms. [S]<list><item>Accept a seated target below 130/80 only without orthostatic symptoms; recheck seated and standing pressures in three weeks.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Lacunar stroke five weeks ago (I69.354)</content>. No new deficit; recovery continuing with physical therapy. [S]<list><item>Continue clopidogrel and atorvastatin.</item><item>Physical therapist informed of the near-fall.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: 2021 Guideline for the Prevention of Stroke in Patients With Stroke and Transient Ischemic Attack (2021); 2025 AHA/ACC/AANP/AAPA/ABC/ACCP/ACPM/AGS/AMA/ASPC/NMA/PCNA/SGIM Guideline for the Prevention, Detection, Evaluation, and Management of High Blood Pressure in Adults (2025); Consensus statement on the definition of orthostatic hypotension, neurally mediated syncope and the postural tachycardia syndrome (2011)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Review in three weeks as planned, with the lipid panel and monitor result. Call 911 for sudden weakness, numbness, facial droop, speech difficulty, or loss of vision, and return the same day for a fall or fainting. Next scheduled visit 1953-08-19: eight-week stroke and blood pressure review with lipid panel and rhythm-monitor results. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
